{"title":"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Four unit squares form a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4c044326e2e84b768dafef07060bd42b0a5cb21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> grid. Each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> unit line segments forming the sides of the squares is colored either red or blue in such a way that each unit square has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> red sides and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> blue sides. One example is shown below (red is solid, blue is dashed). Find the number of such colorings.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the red edges be \"used\" edges. In the digarams below, dashed lines are uncolored lines yet to be decided. Since all four center edges are common to both squares, we consider five distinct cases:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/f/d7fc8bd87f70c04687e145d72c7b03b4d902f80d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Case 1:}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"11\" /> All center edges are used. There is only one way to do this.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/3/443be9ce1c3afc926217b91884d1ed09570c882f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,I; A=(-1,-1);B=(-1,0);C=(-1,1);D=(0,-1);E=(0,0);F=(0,1);G=(1,-1);H=(1,0);I=(1,1); draw(A--C--I--G--cycle,dashed); draw(B--H,red); draw(D--F,red); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/1/331226e700ae378565242419f911b29b000845c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Case 2:}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"11\" /> Three center edges are used, meaning two squares are missing an edge. For each square, there are 2 ways to choose an edge, resulting in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/a/4aae69d5a3cf3e7239ddd216b41562e0c55d903f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> ways. Additionally, considering the rotational symmetry of the arrangement, there are 4 possible rotations, giving a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/541f4f0ac5c46d4e572ab6d69e704f8ad1810583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 4 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> configurations.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/0/780a2ad533f3429ee888b9da342259425467a602.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,I; A=(-1,-1);B=(-1,0);C=(-1,1);D=(0,-1);E=(0,0);F=(0,1);G=(1,-1);H=(1,0);I=(1,1); draw(A--C--I--G--cycle,dashed); draw(B--H,red); draw(D--E,red);draw(E--F,dashed); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/949308f1d0158c4f33a3154470cc9db508bdb248.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Case 3:}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"11\" /> Two center edges are used. There are two sub-cases:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/b/56b89a8d55c98cddce09af9fdbb8bcf116f46cb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Scenario 1:}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"13\" /> The two selected sides are perpendicular to each other. The square diagonally opposite its adjacent square has only one choice, while the other two squares each have two choices. This gives a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/0/c2059dd4d0d2ec5a291b830e2230b46db67e18fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 2 \\times 2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> choices. Considering the 4 possible rotations, the total number of configurations is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/541f4f0ac5c46d4e572ab6d69e704f8ad1810583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 4 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/4/b94384a6db98453198d71cb0220134fec88d7001.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,I; A=(-1,-1);B=(-1,0);C=(-1,1);D=(0,-1);E=(0,0);F=(0,1);G=(1,-1);H=(1,0);I=(1,1); draw(A--C--I--G--cycle,dashed); draw(B--E,red); draw(E--D,red);draw(E--F,dashed);draw(E--H,dashed); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/3/293fb174cfc8cee1417c94dfc253075fc00198b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Scenario 2:}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"13\" /> The two selected sides are aligned along the same straight line. Each of the four squares has 2 choices, yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/2/9521a8469412ce4dd8556ba0edd5af8a8b1ac754.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> possible choices. Taking into account the 2 possible rotations, the total number of configurations is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/9/8e9a2797ecbac08c3a9b93ab5f0cf71575a2cd97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 \\times 2 = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/8/4788e2c3f8025fd099eff883773f876d4717979b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,I; A=(-1,-1);B=(-1,0);C=(-1,1);D=(0,-1);E=(0,0);F=(0,1);G=(1,-1);H=(1,0);I=(1,1); draw(A--C--I--G--cycle,dashed); draw(B--H,red); draw(D--F,dashed); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/d/ced45ddc365d6b23b6cb905528dce1b8b4cd9d47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Case 4:}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" /> Only one center edge is used. This case is similar to Case 2, yielding 16 possible configurations.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c3ff58e907770367369f08b40d9dc4f941707c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,I; A=(-1,-1);B=(-1,0);C=(-1,1);D=(0,-1);E=(0,0);F=(0,1);G=(1,-1);H=(1,0);I=(1,1); draw(A--C--I--G--cycle,dashed); draw(B--E,red); draw(E--D,dashed);draw(E--F,dashed);draw(E--H,dashed); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/8/778f42b8c24f1abc1d3e9f7bd3b2a62f81253381.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Case 5:}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" /> No center edge is used. This is similar to Case 1, with only 1 possible configuration.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/d/cedc52bedc4423d33717dbcf57a0efe64b1db5ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,I; A=(-1,-1);B=(-1,0);C=(-1,1);D=(0,-1);E=(0,0);F=(0,1);G=(1,-1);H=(1,0);I=(1,1); draw(A--C--I--G--cycle,dashed); draw(B--E,dashed); draw(E--D,dashed);draw(E--F,dashed);draw(E--H,dashed); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>In conclusion, the total number of configurations is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/0/9402f6eba4f0b0e66840e184592bd5c54bfe2bc1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 + 16 + 16 + 32 + 16 + 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{082}}\\]\" width=\"265\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Athmyx\">Athmyx</a>\n</p><p>~ LaTeX by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:eevee9406\">eevee9406</a>\n</p><p>~ Additional edits by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Aoum\">aoum</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solutions 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=98hzWL-cUvk&amp;t=6s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=98hzWL-cUvk&amp;t=6s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II\" title=\"2025 AIME II\">2025 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2025\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.ph